.env
# Every per-environment variant too (.env.paseo, .env.summit, …). Upstream ignores only
# bare `.env` and the four `*.local` names above, which would let a `.env.paseo` holding
# real Firebase/TURN values be committed. Build-time values are injected by CI from repo
# variables/secrets (see .github/workflows/release.yaml); `.env.example` stays tracked.
.env.*
!.env.example
